.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-TEST 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-test
.Nd run one of the smoke test suites shipped with kldload against this machine
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar suite
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs a test suite that shipped with the install,
.Pa /usr/local/share/kldload/tests/smoke- Ns Ar suite Ns Pa .sh ,
and returns what it prints and its exit status unchanged.
The suites are the ones kldload's own builds are checked with; each check
prints
.Ql PASS ,
.Ql FAIL
or
.Ql WARN
and the suite ends with a count.
.Pp
Without
.Ar suite ,
.Ql auto
runs the suite for the profile the machine was installed with.
.Pp
The suites need root to look at ZFS, libvirt and the services; run it
with
.Xr sudo 8 .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar suite
Which suite to run; the list is in
.Fl -help .
The usual ones:
.Bl -tag -width "features" -compact
.It Li auto
the suite for this machine's profile
.It Li core , server , desktop , kvm
one profile's suite
.It Li all
every suite
.It Li features
one check for each feature kldload ships, on any profile
.It Li estate
the machines are reachable and monitored, not only listed
.It Li unit , show
the installer's and the first-boot show's own checks
.El
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and the suites installed on this machine, and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/local/share/kldload/tests/
The suites, and
.Pa lib-test.sh ,
which they share.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The suite's own: 0 when nothing failed, and otherwise what the suite
returns, usually 1.
.Nm
itself exits 2 for a suite that is not installed, a name that is not a
plain word, or more than one argument.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-29.
.Ss The suites here (-h, --help)
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-test --help
kldload-test — run a smoke suite against this kldloadOS system

Usage:  sudo kldload-test [SUITE]      (default: auto)
        kldload-test -h | --help       lists the suites installed here

SUITE names a file /usr/local/share/kldload/tests/smoke-<SUITE>.sh, copied
from the repo's tests/ at build time: auto picks by the installed profile;
core, server, desktop, kvm test one profile; all runs everything; features,
estate, unit and show are the narrower ones. The suite's own output and
exit status are what this tool returns.

Exit: the suite's status; 2 when SUITE names no installed file (it used to
      exec a missing path, so `kldload-test dekstop` said "No such file"
      and returned 127, 2026-09-23), a name that is not a plain word, or
      more than one argument. See kldload-test(8).

Suites installed in /usr/local/share/kldload/tests:
  all
  auto
  build
  core
  desktop
  features
  javaapi-rollback
  kvm
  server
  unit
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss A suite (suite)
This machine's older lab machines have no sound device, and the suite
says so:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ sudo kldload-test features

  ── Shipped desktop apps ──────────────────────────────────────────
  ✓ PASS  Timer: binary, launcher and icon all installed
  ✓ PASS  Timer: PyGObject + Gtk4 import on this machine
  ✓ PASS  Timer: .desktop validates

  ── Rollback ──────────────────────────────────────────
  ✓ PASS  rollback is on PATH (/usr/bin/kldload-rollback)
  ✓ PASS  kldload-rollback installed
\&...
  ── Golden images ──────────────────────────────────────────
  ✓ PASS  all 10 golden image(s) carry their @golden snapshot

  ── Guest audio ──────────────────────────────────────────
  ✗ FAIL  guest audio (host half) — no <sound> device: debian-desktop-ud30 klab-blue-centos ...
\&...
  ── WireGuard meshes ──────────────────────────────────────────
  ⚠ WARN  WireGuard — no interfaces up
\&...
  Results:  9 passed  1 failed  2 warnings  (12 total)
\&...
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
The failing line is trimmed; it names 23 machines.
.Ss What it refuses
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-test dekstop
kldload-test: no suite named dekstop (looked for /usr/local/share/kldload/tests/smoke-dekstop.sh)
kldload-test: installed: all auto build core desktop features javaapi-rollback kvm server unit
# (exited 2)
$ kldload-test ../../tmp/x
kldload-test: ../../tmp/x is not a suite name
# (exited 2)
$ kldload-test core extra
kldload-test: one suite at a time (got: core extra)
# (exited 2)
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "kldload-test: no suite named SUITE (looked for PATH)"
Followed by the suites that are installed.
.It "kldload-test: FAIL at line N: COMMAND"
.Nm
itself failed; the suite did not run.
.El
Everything else is the suite's.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-doctor 8 ,
.Xr kldload-estate 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-09-23 a mistyped suite name ran a path that did not exist and
returned 127.
On 2026-09-20 an estate sweep found it had printed
.Dq verified and ready for production
having run no check at all; a missing suite has been fatal since.
On 2026-09-29, writing this page: a suite name was not checked before it
became a path run as root, and a second argument was ignored.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The suites are the copies made when the machine was installed; they are
not updated with the machine.
.Pp
.Ql unit
and
.Ql build
check the installer and the ISO.
On an installed machine the files they check are not there, and they
fail:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ sudo kldload-test unit

  ── mTLS operator CA (kldload-gen-operator-ca) ──
  ✗ operator-CA — tool missing or not executable: /usr/local/share/kldload/tools/kldload-gen-operator-ca
\&...
  1 passed, 7 failed
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Pp
.Nm
compares nothing with a known-good machine; that is
.Xr kldload-doctor 8 .
